--
--
A user-declared destructor must not disable aggregate initialization
of a braced temporary ([dcl.init.aggr]/1, [expr.type.conv]/2); CBMC
routes itert{&g} to constructor overload resolution and fails with
"found no match for symbol 'itert'".  Declaration-form brace init
works; the temporary form is the gap.

FIXED 2026-07-19: synthesized default/copy/move constructors now carry
#is_implicit_ctor (mirroring #is_implicit_dtor) and the braced-
temporary aggregate gate ignores them per [dcl.init.aggr]/1.
